# A side-edge auto-hiding dock in the SWEPT set, one configuration per
# edge, so a size sweep (`mnml-zig test --gate --sizes …`) renders the
# shape the 2026-09-21 grip family lived in. The gate's other files
# drive the editor and the keyboard: none of them puts a dock on a side
# edge, which is why nothing caught three grip-over-a-control bugs
# (hunt/findings-2026-09-21/mouse-SUMMARY.md). Content assertions count
# at 120x40, where they were written; the other rungs prove the frame
# renders, survives the clicks and leaks nothing.
#
# The structural guard proper is `src/app/edge_band_audit.zig` — a hit
# map is not a thing a `.test` can ask about.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
command view.sidebar_mode_auto
# ── the left edge ──
ex dock left
ex dock auto
# Row 19 is the middle of the band at 120x40 — the grip's own rows.
# The grip is in the band's MIDDLE column, so the outermost column is
# band-but-not-grip: inert. Before the side-band rule the grip sat in
# the outermost column instead, on cells that belonged to the activity
# bar and to the editor's scrollbar, and this press pinned the dock.
click 0 19
wait 300
expect screen lacks "dock pinned"
# ── the right edge ──
ex dock right
click 119 19
wait 300
expect screen lacks "dock pinned"
# ── and back to the bottom, where the band is one row and shared ──
ex dock bottom
expect screen contains "alpha"
